[0.008, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[H\r\u001b[12B←  ☒ Headers \u001b[48;2;177;185;249m\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m ☐ Ready proof \r\u001b[6C\u001b[2B\u001b[49m\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m\u001b[1missue excludes cl\u001b[25Gim\u001b[28G, sess\u001b[35Gons, knowledg\u001b[49G, context, events, and next-ta\u001b[80Gk. But deliverabl\u001b[98G #4 says 'ready derivation must be \u001b[22m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m\u001b[1mobservable through the API.' How do you want to pr\u001b[54Gve ready works?\u001b[70GOptions: (a)\u001b[83Gjust GET the task and see status=ready\u001b[122Gafter \u001b[22m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m\u001b[1madd\u001b[7Gng/c\u001b[12Gmpleti\u001b[19Gg deps, or (b) also expose next-task which is the canonical 'what's ready?' query.\r\u001b[5C\u001b[2B\u001b[22m\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mGET\u001b[10Gtask is enough\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mProve ready derivation\u001b[29Gby creating tasks, ad\u001b[51Ging\u001b[55Gdepends_on, and\u001b[71Gche\u001b[75Gking s\u001b[82Ga\u001b[84Gu\u001b[86G tran\u001b[92Gitions via GET /tasks/{id}. N\u001b[122G next-task \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m  \u001b[6G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mendpoint yet.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m2.\u001b[6G\u001b[39mInclude next-task\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  \u001b[6G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mAlso wire"]
[0.000, "o", " up GET /projects/{id}/next-task since it's the natural way to observe readiness and it's a read-only endpoint backed by \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bexisting store logic.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m3. Type something.\r\u001b[1B───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m  4. Chat about this\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mEnter to select · Tab/Arrow keys to navigate · Esc to cancel\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[30;1H\u001b[19;1H\u001b[?2026l"]
