[0.000, "o", "\u001b[39m←\u001b[3G ☒ H\u001b[8Gaders  ☒ Ready proof  ☒ Spec drift \u001b[44G☒ T\u001b[48Gs\u001b[50G tooling \u001b[48;2;177;185;249m\u001b[38;2;0;0;0m ✔ Submit \u001b[49m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m →\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m\u001b[1mReview your answers\u001b[22m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B \u001b[2m│\u001b[22m ● The OpenAPI spec mandates RateLimit-* and Access-Control-Allow-Origin\u001b[76Gheaders\u001b[84Gon\u001b[87GEVERY\u001b[93Gresponse.\u001b[103GContract\u001b[112Gconformance\u001b[124Gtests\u001b[130Gwill\r\u001b[1B \u001b[2m│\u001b[22m   fail without them. Should S4 include tower middleware for rate-limiting and CORS, or do you want the contract tests to skip header\r\u001b[1B \u001b[2m│\u001b[4G\u001b[22m \u001b[6Gvalidation\u001b[17Gfor now?\u001b[K\r\u001b[3C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;78;186;101m→ Add middleware now\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[2m│\u001b[22m ● The issue excludes claims, sessions, knowledge, context, events, and next-task. But deliverable #4 says 'ready derivation must be\r\u001b[1B \u001b[2m│\u001b[22m   observable\u001b[17Gthrough\u001b[25Gthe\u001b[29GAPI.'\u001b[35GHow\u001b[39Gdo\u001b[42Gyou\u001b[46Gwant\u001b[51Gto\u001b[54Gprove\u001b[60Gready\u001b[66Gworks?\u001b[73GOptions:\u001b[82G(a)\u001b[86Gjust\u001b[91GGET\u001b[95Gthe\u001b[99Gtask\u001b["]
