[0.237, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[H\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  · The OpenAPI spec\u001b[25Gmandates RateLimit-* and Access-Control-Allow-Origin\u001b[78Gheaders on EVERY respo\u001b[101Gse. Contract conformance tests will\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bfail without \u001b[20Ghem. Should S4\u001b[35Ginclude to\u001b[46Ge\u001b[48G middleware for rate-limiting and CORS, or do you want the contract tests to skip \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bhead\u001b[11Gr validation for now? →\u001b[35GAdd middleware now\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m· The issue \u001b[19Gxcludes claims, sessions,\u001b[45Gknowledge, context, events, and next-task. But deliverable #4\u001b[107Gsays 'ready deriv\u001b[125Gtion must \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bbe observab\u001b[19G through the API.' How\u001b[42Gdo you\u001b[49Gwan\u001b[53G \u001b[55Go prove ready works? Options: (a) just GET\u001b[98Gth\u001b[101G task\u001b[107Ga\u001b[109Gd se\u001b[115Gsta\u001b[119Gus=ready after \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Badding/comple\u001b[20Ging deps, or\u001b[33G(b) also expose next-task which is the can\u001b[76Gnical 'wh\u001b[86Gt's ready?' query. → Include next-task\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m· I found a\u001b[18Gstruct vs spec drift: ExportDocument in \u001b[59Godel.\u001b[6"]
