[0.000, "o", "──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mThe real question\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BBoth\u001b[8G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249moas3-gen\u001b[17G\u001b[39mand\u001b[21G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mopenapi-to-rust\u001b[37G\u001b[39mgenerate\u001b[46G\u001b[1mseparate wire types from the spec\u001b[22m,\u001b[81Gthen\u001b[86Gyou\u001b[90Gwrite\u001b[96G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mFrom<CoreType>\u001b[111G\u001b[39mconversions\u001b[123G—\u001b[125Gwhich\u001b[131Gis\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bexactly what we already have, except we wrote the wire types by hand instead of generating them.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BSo\u001b[6Gthe\u001b[10Gactual\u001b[17Gtradeoff\u001b[26Gis:\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mCurrent approach (hand-written + contract tests):\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[22m- 9 contract tests already validate responses against\u001b[57Gthe\u001b[61Gspec\u001b[66Gschemas\u001b[30;1H\u001b[27;3H\u001b[?2026l"]
