[0.046, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[H\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;78;186;101m⏺\u001b[39m \u001b[1mFetch\u001b[22m(https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gpu-cli/openapi-to-rust/main/examples/server-openai-responses/src/main.rs)\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  \u001b[39mReceived\u001b[15G\u001b[1m7.8KB\u001b[21G\u001b[22m(200\u001b[26GOK)\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  Allowed by auto mode classifier\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;78;186;101m⏺\u001b[39m \u001b[1mFetch\u001b[22m(https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gpu-cli/openapi-to-rust/main/examples/server-openai-responses/Cargo.toml)\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  \u001b[39mReceived\u001b[15G\u001b[1m1KB\u001b[19G\u001b[22m(200\u001b[24GOK)\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  Allowed by auto mode classifier\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[39m Now I have a thorough understanding\u001b[39Gof\u001b[42Ghow\u001b[46Gopenapi-to-rust\u001b[62Gworks.\u001b[69GLet\u001b[73Gme\u001b[76Gcheck\u001b[82Gone\u001b[86Gmore\u001b[91Gthing\u001b[97G—\u001b[99Gthe\u001b[103Gcurrent\u001b[111Gstate\u001b[117Gof\u001b[120Gour\u001b[124Gbranch:\r\u001b[2B \u001b[3G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mRan \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m⏺ \u001b[39mUser answered Claude's\u001b[26Gquestions:\r\u001b[1B"]
[0.000, "o", "\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  · The S4 PR (#31) is already pushed. Should I retrofit openapi-to-rust into that same PR (amend/force-push), or make it a separate\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mfollow-up PR on a new branch? → Same PR (amend)\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m     \u001b[8G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mop\u001b[11Gnapi-to-rust\u001b[24Ggenerates its own Router via build_rout\u001b[64Gr(). Our curre\u001b[80G router \u001b[89Glso serves /health, /api/v1/openap\u001b[124G.y\u001b[127Gml, \u001b[132Gnd \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mthe UI fallback. Should the gener\u001b[40Gt\u001b[42Gd router be the primary router with our extras merged in, or should we nest the generated \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Brout\u001b[11Gr under /api/v1? → G\u001b[32Gnerated as primary\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[6G\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[30;1H\u001b[27;3H\u001b[?2026l"]
