[0.074, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[H\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[39m Now I ha\u001b[13G a thorough understanding\u001b[39Gof\u001b[42Ghow\u001b[46Gopenapi-to-rust\u001b[62Gworks.\u001b[69GLet\u001b[73Gme\u001b[76Gcheck\u001b[82Gone\u001b[86Gmore\u001b[91Gthing\u001b[97G—\u001b[99Gthe\u001b[103Gcurrent\u001b[111Gstate\u001b[117Gof\u001b[120Gour\u001b[124Gbranch:\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mRan \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m⏺ \u001b[39mUser\u001b[8Ganswered\u001b[17GClaude's\u001b[26Gquestions:\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  · The S4\u001b[15GPR (#31) is already pushed. Should I retrofit openapi-to-rust into that same PR (amend/force-push), or make it a separate\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bfollow-up PR on a new branch? → Same PR (amend)\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m· openapi-to-rust generates its own Router via build_router(). Our current router also serves /health, /api/v1/openapi.yaml, and \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mthe UI fallback. Should the generated r\u001b[47Gter be \u001b[55Ghe primary rou\u001b[70Ger wi\u001b[76Gh our\u001b[82Gextra\u001b[88G \u001b[91Grged in, or should we nest\u001b[118Gthe generat\u001b[130Gd \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;1"]
