[0.118, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[H\r\u001b[2B \u001b[3G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mRan \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m⏺ \u001b[39mUser answered Claude's\u001b[26Gquestions:\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  · The S4 PR (#31) is already pushed. Should I retrofit openapi-to-rust into that same PR (amend/force-push), or make it a separate\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mfollow-up PR on a new branch? → Same PR (amend)\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m     \u001b[8G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mop\u001b[11Gnapi-to-rust\u001b[24Ggenerates its own Router via build_rout\u001b[64Gr(). Our curre\u001b[80G router \u001b[89Glso serves /health, /api/v1/openap\u001b[124G.y\u001b[127Gml, \u001b[132Gnd \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mthe UI fallback. Should the gener\u001b[40Gt\u001b[42Gd router be the primary router with our extras merged in, or should we nest the generated \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Brout\u001b[11Gr under /api/v1? → G\u001b[32Gnerated as primary\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[3G\u001b[39mGood. Now I have everything to write the plan. Let\u001b[54Gme\u001b[57Galso\u001b[62Gquickly\u001b[70Gcheck\u001b[76Gwhat\u001b[81Gtags\u001b[86Gour\u001b[90Goperations\u001b[101Guse\u001b[10"]
